course: dictionary
lesson: 4492
title: Strong feelings and their words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hatred is a very strong feeling of disliking someone or something. It is much stronger than ordinary dislike: you might dislike cold rain, but you do not hate it in the same way. The words around hatred show how strong it is. In «a hatred of spiders», the phrase «a hatred of» tells you the dislike is very strong.
explain: Hatred is a noun, and it usually goes with words like «full of hatred», «hatred of» and «racial hatred». You may also see «love and hatred», which puts two very strong feelings side by side. When you meet a word like this, ask yourself: is the writer describing a small feeling or a very big one?
explain: In everyday talk, people sometimes use hatred lightly, as in «a hatred of broccoli». In serious lessons it means something much more harmful. The sentence «Antisemitism is hatred of Jewish people» shows hatred aimed at a whole group of people, and this kind of hatred is wrong. Learning what the word means helps us speak up against it.
fact: Hatred is a very strong feeling of disliking someone or something.
fact: A hatred of something is a strong dislike of it, as in «a hatred of spiders».
fact: Hatred is much stronger than ordinary dislike.
fact: «Antisemitism is hatred of Jewish people»; it led to the Holocaust, in which about six million Jews were murdered.
fact: Laws forbid stirring up hatred, and religions teach people to replace hatred with love and forgiveness.
exercise: «Antisemitism is hatred of Jewish people.» What does hatred mean here? | A happy surprise | A kind of game | A small, passing worry | *A very strong feeling of disliking
exercise: Which phrase uses hatred in a light, everyday way? | racial hatred | *a hatred of broccoli | love and hatred | full of hatred
exercise: Religions teach people to replace hatred with something else. Which word is the opposite of hatred? | boredom | *love | anger | hunger
test: What does «a hatred of spiders» tell you? | A fear of the dark | A love of spiders | A wish to draw spiders | *A strong dislike of spiders
test: Why do laws forbid stirring up hatred? | Because hatred is always funny | *Because hatred between groups can lead to bullying, violence and war | Because hatred makes people sleepy | Because hatred is a type of weather
exam: Which word is the noun in «full of hatred»? | full | *hatred | of
